### How to use this in your own script

```python
import requests

API_KEY = "<super_api>"
IP_ADDRESS = "178.34.55.101"
LIMIT = 15
CURSOR = "next_set"

url = f"https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/ip_addresses/{IP_ADDRESS}/communicating_files"
params = {"limit": LIMIT, "cursor": CURSOR}
headers = {"x-apikey": API_KEY, "accept": "application/json"}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)
data = response.json()

for file_obj in data["data"]:
    file_id = file_obj["id"]
    context_attrs = file_obj["attributes"]["context_attributes"]
    print(f"File ID: {file_id}")
    print("Context Attributes:")
    for k, v in context_attrs.items():
        print(f"  {k}: {v}")
    print("-" * 40)
```

Replace `<super_api>` with your actual API key. The script will print the IDs and the context attributes for each of the 15 files returned. If you need more than 15, use the `cursor` value from the response (`next_set`) to fetch the next page.
